# M7 red team: IRQControl and IRQHandler attacked from ring 3 with the PIT
# as an interrupt source (user/root/src/redteam/irq.rs); they held. A PIT
# storm on GSI 2 signals at most three times per Ack; an issued GSI cannot
# be issued again through GetIOAPIC; 300 issues of one GSI reuse one
# vector and every GSI can be issued at once; revoking a bound
# notification's untyped empties the IRQ node, so a notification retyped
# at its address is never signalled; and deleting a CNode that holds a
# handler, whose IRQ node holds the last capability to a notification a
# thread waits on, finalises both: the kernel survives, the thread never
# wakes, and the GSI can be issued again.
cmdline: test=redteam-irq
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: root: cmdline "test=redteam-irq"
expect: redteam: irq: a PIT storm at 18.6 kHz on GSI 2 signalled
expect: redteam: irq: 300 issues and deletions of GSI 5 reused IRQ
expect: redteam: irq: revoking N's untyped emptied the IRQ node
expect: redteam: irq: deleting CNode K finalised the handler in it
expect: redteam: irq: every interrupt attack held
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
forbid: KERNEL PANIC
